nes the terms and conditions of issue, conversion, maturity, payment, and interest rate. New issues of Treasury notes mature in 2 to 10 years. Bonds mature in more than 10 years from the issue date. Each outstanding marketable security is listed in the \\\"Monthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States.\\\" The information in this section of the \\\"Treasury Bulletin\\\" pertains only to marketable Treasury securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 575, 798, 971], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"The Bureau of the Fiscal Service is a new bureau within the Treasury Department, formed on October 7, 2012, from the consolidation of the Financial Management Service and the Bureau of the Public Debt. Our mission is to promote the financial integrity and operational efficiency of the U.S. government through exceptional accounting, financing, collections, payments, and shared services. As one bureau, the organization is better positioned to help transform financial management and the delivery of shared services in the federal government. The bureau will be a valued partner for agencies as they work to strengthen their own financial management or as they look for a quality service provider who can allow them to focus on their missions.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 269, 1488, 453], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-1 presents the results of weekly auctions of 4-, 13-, and 26-week bills. Treasury bills mature each Thursday. Issues of 4- and 13-week bills are reopenings of 26-week bills. High rates on accepted tenders and the dollar value of total bids are presented, with the dollar value of awards made on both competitive and noncompetitive basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 453, 1488, 542], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"To encourage the participation of individuals and smaller institutions, Treasury accepts noncompetitive tenders of up to $5 million in each auction of securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 547, 1488, 667], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-2 lists the results of auctions of marketable securities, other than weekly bills, in chronological order over the past 2 years. Issues of cash management bills also are presented.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 669, 1490, 912], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Note: On July 31, 2013, Treasury published amendments to its marketable securities auction rules to accommodate the auction and issuance of Floating Rate Notes (FRNs). An FRN is a security that has an interest payment that can change over time. Treasury FRNs will be indexed to the most recent 13-week Treasury bill auction High Rate, which is the highest accepted discount rate in a Treasury bill auction. FRNs will pay interest quarterly.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [475, 1006, 1155, 1047], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [559, 1075, 1071, 1098], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"[Source: Bureau of the Fiscal Service, Division of Financing Operations]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1120, 322, 1150], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"APRIL\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1179, 718, 1209], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Auction of 69-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1238, 770, 1516], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"On March 30, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $45,000 million of 69-day bills. They were issued April 1 and matured June 9. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $45,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on March 31. Tenders totaled $128,932 million; Treasury accepted $45,000 million, including less than $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.070 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1546, 716, 1579], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Auction of 42-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1610, 770, 1886], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"On March 26, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $60,000 million of 42-day bills. They were issued April 2 and matured May 14. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $60,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on March 31. Tenders totaled $167,417 million; Treasury accepted $60,000 million, including $7 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.080 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1179, 1399, 1212], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1240, 1441, 1518], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"On March 31, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued April 2 and will mature July 30. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 1. Tenders totaled $119,540 million; Treasury accepted $40,001 million, including less than $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.130 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1546, 1386, 1579], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"Auction of 39-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1610, 1441, 1883], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"On March 31, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $45,000 million of 39-day bills. They were issued April 3 and matured May 12. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $45,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 1. Tenders totaled $138,014 million; Treasury accepted $45,000 million, including $3 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.080 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1335, 1968, 1488, 1992], \"page_id\": 36}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [450, 99, 1086, 127], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1299, 97, 1337, 127], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"29\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [386, 193, 1248, 236], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 262, 729, 297], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Auction of 102-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 325, 774, 601], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"On April 1, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 102-day bills. They were issued April 3 and matured July 14. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 2. Tenders totaled $122,269 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including less than $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.125 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 632, 494, 667], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Auction of 3-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 695, 772, 849], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"On April 2, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 3-year notes. The issue was to refund $79,148 million of securities maturing April 15 and to raise new cash of approximately $2,852 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 846, 770, 1030], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"The 3-year notes of Series AL-2023 were dated and issued April 15. They are due April 15, 2023, with interest payable on October 15 and April 15 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/4 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1030, 770, 1494], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon Eastern Time (ET) for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on April 6. Tenders totaled $90,970 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.348 percent with an equivalent price of $99.707782. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.348 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 71.46 percent. The median yield was 0.318 percent, and the low yield was 0.230 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $28 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $39,872 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1492, 774, 1676], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $40,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $132 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for Separate Trading of Registered Interest and Principal Securities (STRIPS) of notes of Series AL-2023 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1702, 772, 1770], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Auction of 9-Year 10-Month 1-1/2 Percent Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1796, 776, 1893], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"On April 2, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $25,000 million of 9-year 10-month 1-1/2 percent notes. The issue was to refund $79,148 million\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 266, 1444, 328], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"of securities maturing April 15 and to raise new cash of approximately $2,852 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 328, 1446, 450], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"The 9-year 10-month 1-1/2 percent notes of Series B-2030 were dated February 15 and issued April 15. They are due February 15, 2030, with interest payable on August 15 and February 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 450, 1448, 938], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on April 7. Tenders totaled $60,846 million; Treasury accepted $25,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.782 percent with an equivalent price of $106.783664. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.782 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 39.03 percent. The median yield was 0.724 percent, and the low yield was 0.080 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $2 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $24,998 million. Accrued interest of $2.47253 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from February 15 to April 15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 938, 1448, 1094], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $25,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $82 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series B-2030 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1122, 1435, 1157], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Auction of 29-Year 10-Month 2 Percent Bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1188, 1446, 1336], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"On April 2, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $17,000 million of 29-year 10-month 2 percent bonds. The issue was to refund $79,148 million of securities maturing April 15 and to raise new cash of approximately $2,852 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1341, 1448, 1464], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"The 29-year 10-month 2 percent bonds of February 2050 were dated February 15 and issued April 15. They are due February 15, 2050, with interest payable on August 15 and February 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1466, 1444, 1890], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the bonds before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on April 8. Tenders totaled $39,983 million; Treasury accepted $17,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 1.325 percent with an equivalent price of $116.588638. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 1.325 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 18.15 percent. The median yield was 1.270 percent, and the low yield was 0.080 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $4 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $16,997 million. Accrued interest of $3.29670\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1284, 1992, 1443, 2022], \"page_id\": 37}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [211, 99, 246, 130], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"30\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [475, 94, 1109, 127], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [382, 189, 1248, 236], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 264, 772, 325], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"per $1,000 must be paid for the period from February 15 to April 15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 325, 774, 486], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $17,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $56 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of bonds of February 2050 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 504, 734, 542], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 566, 772, 851], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"On March 31, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued April 7 and will mature September 8. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 2. Tenders totaled $115,885 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $5 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.150 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 872, 718, 912], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Auction of 43-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 936, 772, 1219], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"On April 3, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $60,000 million of 43-day bills. They were issued April 8 and matured May 21. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $60,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 6. Tenders totaled $189,020 million; Treasury accepted $60,000 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.095 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 1242, 718, 1280], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Auction of 69-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1301, 772, 1586], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"On April 6, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $45,000 million of 69-day bills. They were issued April 8 and matured June 16. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $45,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 7. Tenders totaled $121,993 million; Treasury accepted $45,000 million, including less than $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.135 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 1608, 732, 1648], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 1669, 772, 1898], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"On April 3, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued April 9 and will mature August 6. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 7. Tenders totaled $109,788 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $6 million of noncompetitive\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 262, 1441, 328], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.180 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 351, 1404, 391], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Auction of 103-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 412, 1444, 698], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"On April 7, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 103-day bills. They were issued April 9 and will mature July 21. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 8. Tenders totaled $111,606 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $4 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.200 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 719, 1390, 757], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Auction of 40-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 783, 1446, 1063], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"On April 7, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $45,000 million of 40-day bills. They were issued April 9 and matured May 19. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $45,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 8. Tenders totaled $119,378 million; Treasury accepted $45,000 million, including less than $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.160 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1089, 1404, 1124], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1153, 1444, 1433], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"On April 7, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued April 14 and will mature September 15. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 8. Tenders totaled $104,114 million; Treasury accepted $40,001 million, including $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.250 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1459, 1390, 1497], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"Auction of 69-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1518, 1444, 1801], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"On April 9, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $35,000 million of 69-day bills. They were issued April 15 and matured June 23. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $35,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 13. Tenders totaled $112,711 million; Treasury accepted $35,000 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.270 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [228, 1989, 388, 2022], \"page_id\": 38}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [450, 94, 1089, 130], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1293, 92, 1335, 130], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"31\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [386, 189, 1248, 233], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 262, 718, 299], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Auction of 43-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 323, 776, 603], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"On April 9, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $65,000 million of 43-day bills. They were issued April 15 and matured May 28. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $65,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 14. Tenders totaled $202,937 million; Treasury accepted $65,000 million, including $12 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.190 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 629, 734, 667], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 693, 776, 971], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"On April 9, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $25,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued April 16 and will mature August 13. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $25,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 14. Tenders totaled $103,369 million; Treasury accepted $25,000 million, including $13 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.220 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 995, 734, 1035], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Auction of 103-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1058, 778, 1341], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"On April 14, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 103-day bills. They were issued April 16 and will mature July 28. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 15. Tenders totaled $99,621 million; Treasury accepted $30,000 million, including less than $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.165 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1362, 736, 1402], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1426, 776, 1709], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"On April 14, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued April 21 and will mature September 22. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 15. Tenders totaled $94,066 million; Treasury accepted $30,000 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.190 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1730, 719, 1770], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Auction of 43-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1794, 774, 1921], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"On April 16, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $65,000 million of 43-day bills. They were issued April 22 and matured June 4. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $65,000 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 262, 1446, 422], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Treasury auctioned the bills on April 20. Tenders totaled $187,663 million; Treasury accepted $65,000 million, including $11 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.120 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 446, 1406, 481], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 507, 1444, 790], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"On April 16, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $25,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued April 23 and will mature August 20. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $25,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 21. Tenders totaled $87,716 million; Treasury accepted $25,000 million, including $28 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.110 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 811, 1175, 849], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Auction of 52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 874, 1448, 1186], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"On April 16, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $28,000 million of 364-day Treasury bills. They were issued April 23 and will mature April 22, 2021. The issue was to refund $96,775 million of all maturing bills and to raise new cash of approximately $91,225 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 21. Tenders totaled $94,594 million; Treasury accepted $28,000 million, including $209 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.165 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1186, 1444, 1275], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $28,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $2,955 million from FRBs for their own accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1304, 1444, 1370], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Auction of 5-Year Treasury Inflation Protected Security (TIPS)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1398, 1448, 1553], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"On April 16, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $17,000 million of 5-year TIPS. The issue was to refund $137,570 million of securities maturing April 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $21,430 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1553, 1446, 1735], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"The 5-year TIPS of Series X-2025 were dated April 15 and issued April 30. They are due April 15, 2025, with interest payable on October 15 and April 15 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1735, 1446, 1921], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the TIPS before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on April 23. Tenders totaled $46,589 million; Treasury accepted $17,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1282, 1989, 1444, 2018], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [215, 97, 251, 125], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"32\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [475, 99, 1109, 127], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [384, 196, 1246, 231], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 264, 770, 691], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"yield of -0.320 percent with an equivalent adjusted price of $102.366204. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than -0.320 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 61.18 percent. The median yield was -0.375 percent, and the low yield was -0.880 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $75 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $16,925 million. Adjusted accrued interest of $0.05130 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from April 15 to April 30. Both the unadjusted price of $102.226154 and the unadjusted accrued interest of $0.05123 were adjusted by an index ratio of 1.00137, for the period from April 15 to April 30.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 693, 772, 846], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $17,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $1,476 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of TIPS of Series X-2025 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 872, 734, 910], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Auction of 103-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 938, 774, 1219], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"On April 21, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 103-day bills. They were issued April 23 and will mature August 4. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 22. Tenders totaled $93,008 million; Treasury accepted $30,000 million, including $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.105 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1245, 730, 1280], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1306, 772, 1586], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"On April 21, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued April 28 and will mature September 29. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 22. Tenders totaled $92,360 million; Treasury accepted $30,000 million, including $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.135 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1610, 494, 1645], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 1676, 772, 1827], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"On April 23, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $42,000 million of 2-year notes. The issue was to refund $137,570 million of securities maturing April 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $21,430 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1827, 772, 1923], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"The 2-year notes of Series AZ-2022 were dated and issued April 30. They are due April 30, 2022, with interest payable on October 31 and April 30 until\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 264, 1446, 356], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 356, 1446, 785], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 11:00 a.m. ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 11:30 a.m. ET for competitive tenders on April 27. Tenders totaled $130,295 million; Treasury accepted $42,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.229 percent with an equivalent price of $99.792594. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.229 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 72.96 percent. The median yield was 0.185 percent, and the low yield was 0.080 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $112 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $41,788 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 785, 1448, 943], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $42,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $3,647 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series AZ-2022 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 969, 1162, 1002], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Auction of 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1032, 1444, 1183], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"On April 23, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $43,000 million of 5-year notes. The issue was to refund $137,570 million of securities maturing April 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $21,430 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1186, 1446, 1370], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"The 5-year notes of Series Y-2025 were dated and issued April 30. They are due April 30, 2025, with interest payable on October 31 and April 30 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-3/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1370, 1446, 1798], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on April 27. Tenders totaled $117,697 million; Treasury accepted $43,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.394 percent with an equivalent price of $99.906021. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.394 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 49.71 percent. The median yield was 0.350 percent, and the low yield was 0.080 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $16 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $42,984 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1798, 1444, 1890], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $43,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $3,734 million from FRBs for their own accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [226, 1992, 390, 2020], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [444, 94, 1091, 130], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1297, 99, 1333, 125], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"33\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [384, 189, 1248, 238], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 264, 772, 328], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series Y-2025 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 356, 494, 389], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Auction of 7-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 417, 772, 573], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"On April 23, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $35,000 million of 7-year notes. The issue was to refund $137,570 million of securities maturing April 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $21,430 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 573, 774, 757], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"The 7-year notes of Series K-2027 were dated and issued April 30. They are due April 30, 2027, with interest payable on October 31 and April 30 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/2 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 754, 774, 1186], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on April 28. Tenders totaled $89,758 million; Treasury accepted $35,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.525 percent with an equivalent price of $99.828398. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.525 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 26.91 percent. The median yield was 0.470 percent, and the low yield was 0.080 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $6 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $34,994 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 1186, 772, 1339], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $35,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $3,040 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series K-2027 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 1365, 760, 1405], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Floating Rate Notes (FRNs)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1431, 774, 1584], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"On April 23, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $22,000 million of 2-year FRNs. The issue was to refund $137,570 million of securities maturing April 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $21,430 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1582, 774, 1770], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"The 2-year FRNs of Series BA-2022 were dated and issued April 30. They are due April 30, 2022, with interest payable on July 31, October 31, January 31, and April 30 until maturity. Treasury set a spread of 0.114 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a discount margin basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1768, 776, 1921], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the FRNs before 11:00 a.m. ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 11:30 a.m. ET for competitive tenders on April 28. Tenders totaled $66,362 million; Treasury accepted $22,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 264, 1448, 570], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high discount margin of 0.114 percent with an equivalent price of $100.000000. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at discount margins lower than 0.114 percent. Tenders at the high discount margin were allotted 33.89 percent. The median discount margin was 0.101 percent, and the low discount margin was 0.070 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $21 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $21,979 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 575, 1444, 667], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $22,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $1,911 million from FRBs for their own accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 688, 1395, 731], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Auction of 43-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 754, 1446, 1037], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"On April 23, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $55,000 million of 43-day bills. They were issued April 29 and matured June 11. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $55,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 28. Tenders totaled $177,092 million; Treasury accepted $55,001 million, including $12 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.085 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1056, 1404, 1098], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1120, 1448, 1405], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"On April 23, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $25,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued April 30 and will mature August 27. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $25,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 29. Tenders totaled $87,520 million; Treasury accepted $25,001 million, including $4 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.110 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1428, 1408, 1466], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Auction of 273-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1492, 1448, 1770], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"On April 23, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $25,000 million of 273-day bills. They were issued April 30 and will mature January 28, 2021. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $25,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 29. Tenders totaled $74,413 million; Treasury accepted $25,000 million, including $4 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.165 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1796, 1410, 1836], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Auction of 103-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1860, 1444, 1923], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"On April 28, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 103-day bills. They were\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1284, 1992, 1446, 2022], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [209, 92, 257, 127], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"34\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [472, 92, 1111, 127], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [375, 189, 1255, 238], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [182, 264, 778, 483], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"issued April 30 and will mature August 11. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 29. Tenders totaled $91,592 million; Treasury accepted $30,000 million, including $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.115 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [182, 533, 290, 575], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"MAY\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 589, 736, 632], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [180, 653, 783, 938], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"On April 28, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued May 5 and will mature October 6. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on April 30. Tenders totaled $86,975 million; Treasury accepted $30,000 million, including $5 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.140 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 959, 683, 1002], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Auction of 105-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [180, 1025, 783, 1308], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"On April 30, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 105-day bills. They were issued May 5 and will mature August 18. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 4. Tenders totaled $100,534 million; Treasury accepted $30,000 million, including $5 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.115 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1325, 741, 1370], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 1388, 781, 1671], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"On April 30, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued May 7 and will mature September 3. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 5. Tenders totaled $101,400 million; Treasury accepted $30,000 million, including $14 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.130 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 1690, 719, 1732], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Auction of 42-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [182, 1754, 778, 1919], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"On April 30, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $65,000 million of 42-day bills. They were issued May 7 and matured June 18. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $65,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 5. Tenders totaled\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 262, 1466, 394], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"$178,384 million; Treasury accepted $65,000 million, including $10 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.115 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [854, 415, 1408, 453], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [854, 476, 1455, 761], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"On May 5, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $35,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued May 12 and will mature October 13. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $35,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 6. Tenders totaled $101,943 million; Treasury accepted $35,000 million, including less than $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.150 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 780, 1404, 827], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Auction of 105-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [852, 842, 1459, 1129], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"On May 5, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 105-day bills. They were issued May 12 and will mature August 25. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 7. Tenders totaled $90,099 million; Treasury accepted $30,000 million, including $4 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.125 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1153, 1180, 1188], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"May Quarterly Financing\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1216, 1461, 1400], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"On May 6, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $42,000 million of 3-year notes, $32,000 million of 10-year notes, and $22,000 million of 30-year bonds to refund $56,961 million of securities maturing May 15, 2020 and to raise new cash of approximately $39,039 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1400, 1455, 1584], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"The 3-year notes of Series AM-2023 were dated and issued May 15. They are due May 15, 2023, with interest payable on November 15 and May 15 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [854, 1584, 1459, 1923], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on May 11. Tenders totaled $106,872 million; Treasury accepted $42,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.230 percent with an equivalent price of $99.686264. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.230 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 29.24 percent. The median yield was 0.199 percent, and the low yield was 0.080\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [228, 1992, 390, 2025], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [450, 92, 1082, 127], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1293, 94, 1333, 127], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"35\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [386, 191, 1244, 231], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 262, 770, 358], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $29 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $41,968 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 356, 769, 509], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $42,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $22,212 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series AM-2023 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 504, 770, 693], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"The 10-year notes of Series C-2030 were dated and issued May 15. They are due May 15, 2030, with interest payable on November 15 and May 15 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-5/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 695, 776, 1124], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on May 12. Tenders totaled $85,964 million; Treasury accepted $32,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.700 percent with an equivalent price of $99.276869. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.700 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 28.91 percent. The median yield was 0.650 percent, and the low yield was 0.590 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $11 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $31,989 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1122, 774, 1278], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $32,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $16,923 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series C-2030 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 1278, 774, 1461], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"The 30-year bonds of May 2050 were dated and issued May 15. They are due May 15, 2050, with interest payable on November 15 and May 15 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 1-1/4 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1464, 770, 1890], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the bonds before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on May 13. Tenders totaled $50,631 million; Treasury accepted $22,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 1.342 percent with an equivalent price of $97.734134. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 1.342 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 98.50 percent. The median yield was 1.279 percent, and the low yield was 0.080 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $6 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $21,994 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 264, 1444, 417], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $22,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $11,635 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of bonds of May 2050 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 446, 1406, 481], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 514, 1443, 787], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"On May 7, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $35,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued May 14 and will mature September 10. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $35,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 12. Tenders totaled $118,252 million; Treasury accepted $35,001 million, including $10 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.145 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 813, 1393, 849], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"Auction of 42-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 874, 1444, 1155], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"On May 7, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $65,000 million of 42-day bills. They were issued May 14 and matured June 25. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $65,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 12. Tenders totaled $190,583 million; Treasury accepted $65,001 million, including $6 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.110 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1179, 1406, 1219], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"Auction of 105-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1245, 1443, 1523], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"On May 12, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $35,000 million of 105-day bills. They were issued May 19 and will mature September 1. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $35,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 13. Tenders totaled $122,801 million; Treasury accepted $35,000 million, including $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.140 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1549, 1408, 1584], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1612, 1443, 1893], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"On May 12, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued May 19 and will mature October 20. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 13. Tenders totaled $118,961 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.155 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1284, 1989, 1443, 2018], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [220, 97, 246, 123], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"36\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [477, 94, 1106, 123], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [384, 193, 1244, 231], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 262, 730, 297], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 328, 774, 601], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"On May 14, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued May 21 and will mature September 17. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 19. Tenders totaled $123,878 million; Treasury accepted $40,002 million, including $6 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.140 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 632, 718, 665], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"Auction of 42-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 695, 772, 969], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"On May 14, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $65,000 million of 42-day bills. They were issued May 21 and matured July 2. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $65,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 19. Tenders totaled $188,502 million; Treasury accepted $65,000 million, including $6 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.105 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 999, 497, 1030], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"Auction of 52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1061, 770, 1367], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"On May 14, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $31,000 million of 364-day Treasury bills. They were issued May 21 and will mature May 20, 2021. The issue was to refund $153,840 million of all maturing bills and to raise new cash of approximately $99,160 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 19. Tenders totaled $102,358 million; Treasury accepted $31,000 million, including $219 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.160 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1367, 769, 1461], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $31,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $4,161 million from FRBs for their own accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [193, 1490, 756, 1523], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"Auction of 9-Year 8-Month 0-1/8 Percent TIPS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [193, 1553, 770, 1674], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"On May 14, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $12,000 million of 9-year 8-month 0-1/8 percent TIPS. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $32,000 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1676, 770, 1796], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"The 9-year 8-month 0-1/8 percent TIPS of Series A-2030 were dated January 15 and issued May 29. They are due January 15, 2030, with interest payable on July 15 and January 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1798, 770, 1923], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the TIPS before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on May 21. Tenders totaled $28,737 million; Treasury accepted\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 262, 1443, 785], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"$12,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of -0.470 percent with an equivalent adjusted price of $106.232149. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than -0.470 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 29.48 percent. The median yield was -0.557 percent, and the low yield was -0.610 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $34 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $11,966 million. Adjusted accrued interest of $0.46519 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from January 15 to May 29. Both the unadjusted price of $105.867963 and the unadjusted accrued interest of $0.46360 were adjusted by an index ratio of 1.00344, for the period from January 15 to May 29. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of TIPS of Series A-2030 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 816, 1402, 846], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"Auction of 105-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [863, 877, 1443, 1155], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"On May 19, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 105-day bills. They were issued May 26 and will mature September 8. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 20. Tenders totaled $121,585 million; Treasury accepted $40,001 million, including $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.140 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1183, 1404, 1219], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1245, 1443, 1523], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"On May 19, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued May 26 and will mature October 27. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 20. Tenders totaled $117,167 million; Treasury accepted $40,001 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.150 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [863, 1551, 1390, 1584], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"Auction of 42-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1612, 1443, 1893], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"On May 21, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $65,000 million of 42-day bills. They were issued May 28 and matured July 9. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $65,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 26. Tenders totaled $184,267 million; Treasury accepted $65,001 million, including $4 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.120 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [233, 1994, 388, 2018], \"page_id\": 44}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [450, 97, 1091, 127], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1293, 94, 1335, 130], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"37\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [384, 193, 1250, 233], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 262, 734, 297], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 325, 774, 601], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"On May 21, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued May 28 and will mature September 24. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 27. Tenders totaled $109,816 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $14 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.170 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 632, 710, 695], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Auction of 1-Year 11-Month 0.114 Percent FRNs\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 724, 772, 846], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"On May 21, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $20,000 million of 1-year 11-month 0.114 percent FRNs. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $32,000 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 846, 774, 997], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"The 1-year 11-month 0.114 percent FRNs of Series BA-2022 were dated April 30 and issued May 29. They are due April 30, 2022, with interest payable on July 31, October 31, January 31, and April 30 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 999, 778, 1523], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the FRNs before 11:00 a.m. ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 11:30 a.m. ET for competitive tenders on May 27. Tenders totaled $62,315 million; Treasury accepted $20,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high discount margin of 0.098 percent with an equivalent price of $100.031070. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at discount margins lower than 0.098 percent. Tenders at the high discount margin were allotted 51.46 percent. The median discount margin was 0.090 percent, and the low discount margin was 0.040 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $7 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $19,993 million. Accrued interest of $0.019047505 per $100 must be paid for the period from April 30 to May 29.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1553, 732, 1589], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Auction of 273-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 1612, 770, 1893], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"On May 21, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $25,000 million of 273-day bills. They were issued May 28 and will mature February 25, 2021. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $25,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 27. Tenders totaled $79,271 million; Treasury accepted $25,000 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.180 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 264, 978, 297], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"JUNE\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 323, 1188, 358], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Auction of 20-Year Bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 387, 1443, 540], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"On May 14, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $20,000 million of 20-year bonds. The issue was to refund $87,288 million of securities maturing May 31 and to raise new cash of approximately $59,712 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 540, 1446, 726], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"The 20-year bonds of May 2040 were dated May 15 and issued June 1. They are due May 15, 2040, with interest payable on November 15 and May 15 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 1-1/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 726, 1444, 1209], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the bonds before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on May 20. Tenders totaled $50,629 million; Treasury accepted $20,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 1.220 percent with an equivalent price of $98.321703. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 1.220 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 8.25 percent. The median yield was 1.159 percent, and the low yield was 0.088 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $6 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $19,994 million. Accrued interest of $0.51970 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from May 15 to June 1.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1214, 1448, 1367], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $20,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $2,100 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of bonds of May 2040 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1395, 1164, 1428], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1459, 1446, 1612], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"On May 21, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $44,000 million of 2-year notes. The issue was to refund $87,288 million of securities maturing May 31 and to raise new cash of approximately $59,712 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1615, 1444, 1794], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"The 2-year notes of Series BB-2022 were dated May 31 and issued June 1. They are due May 31, 2022, with interest payable on November 30 and May 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1798, 1446, 1921], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on May 26. Tenders totaled $118,050 million; Treasury accepted\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1286, 1992, 1446, 2020], \"page_id\": 45}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [209, 92, 251, 132], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"38\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [466, 87, 1111, 130], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [375, 184, 1255, 240], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [180, 266, 778, 632], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"$44,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.178 percent with an equivalent price of $99.894379. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.178 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 18.84 percent. The median yield was 0.147 percent, and the low yield was 0.018 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $110 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $43,790 million. Accrued interest of $0.00342 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from May 31 to June 1.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [178, 636, 781, 787], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $44,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $4,619 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series BB-2022 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [182, 813, 494, 849], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Auction of 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 872, 783, 1032], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"On May 21, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $45,000 million of 5-year notes. The issue was to refund $87,288 million of securities maturing May 31 and to raise new cash of approximately $59,712 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 1035, 780, 1214], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"The 5-year notes of Series Z-2025 were dated May 31 and issued June 1. They are due May 31, 2025, with interest payable on November 30 and May 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/4 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [182, 1216, 785, 1702], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on May 27. Tenders totaled $102,790 million; Treasury accepted $45,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.334 percent with an equivalent price of $99.584056. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.334 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 36.96 percent. The median yield was 0.280 percent, and the low yield was 0.088 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $17 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $44,983 million. Accrued interest of $0.00683 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from May 31 to June 1.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 1707, 781, 1857], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $45,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $4,724 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series Z-2025 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 257, 1168, 297], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Auction of 7-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 328, 1446, 478], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"On May 21, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $38,000 million of 7-year notes. The issue was to refund $87,288 million of securities maturing May 31 and to raise new cash of approximately $59,712 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 481, 1446, 665], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"The 7-year notes of Series L-2027 were dated May 31 and issued June 1. They are due May 31, 2027, with interest payable on November 30 and May 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/2 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [854, 665, 1446, 1155], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on May 28. Tenders totaled $96,810 million; Treasury accepted $38,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.553 percent with an equivalent price of $99.636717. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.553 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 42.30 percent. The median yield was 0.500 percent, and the low yield was 0.420 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $9 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $37,991 million. Accrued interest of $0.01366 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from May 31 to June 1.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1157, 1446, 1308], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $38,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $3,989 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series L-2027 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1334, 1402, 1370], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Auction of 105-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1400, 1450, 1678], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"On May 26, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 105-day bills. They were issued June 2 and will mature September 15. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 27. Tenders totaled $122,420 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.165 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1707, 1408, 1737], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1761, 1450, 1921], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"On May 26, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued June 2 and will mature November 3. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on May 28.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [220, 1992, 406, 2022], \"page_id\": 46}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [448, 97, 1091, 132], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1293, 92, 1335, 130], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"39\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [384, 191, 1250, 236], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 259, 776, 391], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"Tenders totaled $126,491 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $9 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.170 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 415, 736, 450], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 471, 774, 759], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"On May 28, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued June 4 and will mature October 1. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 2. Tenders totaled $124,185 million; Treasury accepted $40,001 million, including $19 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.165 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 780, 719, 818], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"Auction of 42-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 844, 774, 1129], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"On May 28, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $65,000 million of 42-day bills. They were issued June 4 and will mature July 16. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $65,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 2. Tenders totaled $184,157 million; Treasury accepted $65,002 million, including $24 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.135 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1146, 736, 1188], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"Auction of 105-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1214, 774, 1494], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"On June 2, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 105-day bills. They were issued June 9 and will mature September 22. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 3. Tenders totaled $130,141 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including less than $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.170 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1518, 734, 1556], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1582, 772, 1862], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"On June 2, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued June 9 and will mature November 10. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 3. Tenders totaled $124,527 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $4 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.180 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 262, 1408, 299], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 323, 1443, 606], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"On June 4, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued June 11 and will mature October 8. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 9. Tenders totaled $132,065 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $28 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.185 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 627, 1392, 667], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"Auction of 42-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 693, 1444, 976], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"On June 4, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $60,000 million of 42-day bills. They were issued June 11 and will mature July 23. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $60,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 9. Tenders totaled $162,171 million; Treasury accepted $60,000 million, including $12 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.165 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 995, 1166, 1035], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"Auction of 3-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1058, 1446, 1216], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"On June 4, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $44,000 million of 3-year notes. The issue was to refund $22,692 million of securities maturing June 15 and to raise new cash of approximately $69,308 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1216, 1446, 1400], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"The 3-year notes of Series AN-2023 were dated and issued June 15. They are due June 15, 2023, with interest payable on December 15 and June 15 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/4 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1398, 1448, 1827], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on June 8. Tenders totaled $112,001 million; Treasury accepted $44,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.280 percent with an equivalent price of $99.910439. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.280 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 99.87 percent. The median yield was 0.240 percent, and the low yield was 0.080 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $17 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $43,983 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1827, 1446, 1923], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $44,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $626 million from FRBs for their own accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1284, 1989, 1446, 2022], \"page_id\": 47}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [215, 99, 251, 130], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"40\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [472, 94, 1113, 127], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [386, 191, 1244, 236], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 264, 774, 328], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series AN-2023 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 356, 709, 417], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Auction of 9-Year 11-Month 0-5/8 Percent Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 446, 770, 601], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"On June 4, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $29,000 million of 9-year 11-month 0-5/8 percent notes. The issue was to refund $22,692 million of securities maturing June 15 and to raise new cash of approximately $69,308 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 603, 769, 724], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"The 9-year 11-month 0-5/8 percent notes of Series C-2030 were dated May 15 and issued June 15. They are due May 15, 2030, with interest payable on November 15 and May 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 726, 774, 1214], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on June 9. Tenders totaled $65,653 million; Treasury accepted $29,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.832 percent with an equivalent price of $98.033536. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.832 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 52.09 percent. The median yield was 0.769 percent, and the low yield was 0.700 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $1 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $28,999 million. Accrued interest of $0.52649 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from May 15 to June 15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1214, 770, 1372], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $29,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $412 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series C-2030 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 1398, 718, 1461], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Auction of 29-Year 11-Month 1-1/4 Percent Bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1494, 769, 1645], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"On June 4, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $19,000 million of 29-year 11-month 1-1/4 percent bonds. The issue was to refund $22,692 million of securities maturing June 15 and to raise new cash of approximately $69,308 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1645, 770, 1768], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"The 29-year 11-month 1-1/4 percent bonds of May 2050 were dated May 15 and issued June 15. They are due May 15, 2050, with interest payable on November 15 and May 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1768, 772, 1923], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the bonds before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on June 11. Tenders totaled $43,715 million; Treasury accepted $19,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 264, 1444, 603], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 1.450 percent with an equivalent price of $95.158932. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 1.450 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 62.36 percent. The median yield was 1.380 percent, and the low yield was 0.880 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $1 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $18,999 million. Accrued interest of $1.05299 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from May 15 to June 15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 606, 1444, 757], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $19,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $270 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of bonds of May 2050 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 785, 1406, 818], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Auction of 105-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 844, 1444, 1124], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"On June 9, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $35,000 million of 105-day bills. They were issued June 16 and will mature September 29. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $35,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 10. Tenders totaled $122,334 million; Treasury accepted $35,001 million, including $7 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.180 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 1155, 1408, 1188], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1212, 1446, 1494], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"On June 9, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued June 16 and will mature November 17. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 10. Tenders totaled $118,154 million; Treasury accepted $40,001 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.190 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1520, 1406, 1556], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1584, 1444, 1860], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"On June 11, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued June 18 and will mature October 15. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 16. Tenders totaled $134,612 million; Treasury accepted $40,000 million, including $12 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.180 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [228, 1994, 390, 2018], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [450, 97, 1082, 127], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1295, 97, 1330, 125], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"41\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [386, 189, 1240, 231], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 264, 718, 292], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 42-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 328, 770, 603], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On June 11, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $50,000 million of 42-day bills. They were issued June 18 and will mature July 30. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $50,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 16. Tenders totaled $141,076 million; Treasury accepted $50,001 million, including $27 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.150 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 632, 495, 665], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 52-Week Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 695, 770, 997], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On June 11, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $34,000 million of 364-day Treasury bills. They were issued June 18 and will mature June 17, 2021. The issue was to refund $152,824 million of all maturing bills and to raise new cash of approximately $85,176 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 16. Tenders totaled $98,916 million; Treasury accepted $34,000 million, including $224 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.200 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1002, 770, 1091], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $34,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $4,054 million from FRBs for their own accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1120, 730, 1153], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 105-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1183, 770, 1459], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On June 16, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $35,000 million of 105-day bills. They were issued June 23 and will mature October 6. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $35,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 17. Tenders totaled $113,804 million; Treasury accepted $35,001 million, including $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.170 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1490, 730, 1523], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1553, 770, 1829], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On June 16, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued June 23 and will mature November 24. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 17. Tenders totaled $128,745 million; Treasury accepted $40,001 million, including $1 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.185 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 264, 1404, 297], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 119-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 328, 1441, 603], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On June 18, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 119-day bills. They were issued June 25 and will mature October 22. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 23. Tenders totaled $133,271 million; Treasury accepted $40,001 million, including $10 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.155 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 632, 1401, 665], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 273-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 695, 1443, 971], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On June 18, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $20,000 million of 273-day bills. They were issued June 25 and will mature March 25, 2021. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $20,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 23. Tenders totaled $70,649 million; Treasury accepted $20,000 million, including $4 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.180 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 999, 1386, 1032], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 42-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1063, 1441, 1339], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On June 18, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $40,000 million of 42-day bills. They were issued June 25 and will mature August 6. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $40,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 23. Tenders totaled $127,959 million; Treasury accepted $40,001 million, including $11 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.125 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1367, 1443, 1428], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Auction of 19-Year 11-Month 1-1/8 Percent Bonds\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1459, 1443, 1615], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"On June 11, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $17,000 million of 19-year 11-month 1-1/8 percent bonds. The issue was to refund $79,521 million of securities maturing June 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $86,479 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1615, 1443, 1735], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"The 19-year 11-month 1-1/8 percent bonds of May 2040 were dated May 15 and issued June 30. They are due May 15, 2040, with interest payable on November 15 and May 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 1735, 1444, 1919], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the bonds before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on June 17. Tenders totaled $44,747 million; Treasury accepted $17,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1286, 1994, 1446, 2020], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [209, 90, 253, 127], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"42\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [466, 87, 1124, 134], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [381, 191, 1259, 236], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [175, 250, 778, 568], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"yield of 1.314 percent with an equivalent price of $96.702809. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 1.314 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 54.47 percent. The median yield was 1.260 percent, and the low yield was 0.880 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $1 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $16,999 million. Accrued interest of $1.40625 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from May 15 to June 30.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [180, 568, 780, 731], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $17,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $2,325 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of bonds of May 2040 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [186, 752, 778, 790], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Auction of 4-Year 10-Month 0-1/8 Percent TIPS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 811, 785, 966], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"On June 11, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $15,000 million of 4-year 10-month 0-1/8 percent TIPS. The issue was to refund $79,521 million of securities maturing June 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $86,479 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [180, 964, 783, 1091], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The 4-year 10-month 0-1/8 percent TIPS of Series X-2025 were dated April 15 and issued June 30. They are due April 15, 2025, with interest payable on October 15 and April 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [182, 1091, 781, 1702], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the TIPS before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on June 18. Tenders totaled $41,759 million; Treasury accepted $15,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of -0.766 percent with an equivalent adjusted price of $103.608385. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than -0.766 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 36.59 percent. The median yield was -0.816 percent, and the low yield was -0.880 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $41 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $14,959 million. Adjusted accrued interest of $0.25770 per $1,000 must be paid for the period from April 15 to June 30. Both the unadjusted price of $104.357673 and the unadjusted accrued interest of $0.25956 were adjusted by an index ratio of 0.99282, for the period from April 15 to June 30.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [178, 1704, 785, 1862], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $15,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $2,052 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of TIPS of Series X-2025 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 264, 1452, 328], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Auction of 1-Year 10-Month 0.114 Percent FRNs\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [849, 354, 1452, 481], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"On June 18, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $20,000 million of 1-year 10-month 0.114 percent FRNs. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $20,000 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [852, 481, 1457, 629], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The 1-year 10-month 0.114 percent FRNs of Series BA-2022 were dated April 30 and issued June 26. They are due April 30, 2022, with interest payable on July 31, October 31, January 31, and April 30 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [849, 632, 1459, 1155], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the FRNs before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on June 24. Tenders totaled $63,115 million; Treasury accepted $20,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high discount margin of 0.080 percent with an equivalent price of $100.063394. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at discount margins lower than 0.080 percent. Tenders at the high discount margin were allotted 89.45 percent. The median discount margin was 0.075 percent, and the low discount margin was 0.050 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $11 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $19,989 million. Accrued interest of $0.040280294 per $100 must be paid for the period from April 30 to June 26.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [852, 1181, 1180, 1221], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1242, 1450, 1395], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"On June 18, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $46,000 million of 2-year notes. The issue was to refund $79,521 million of securities maturing June 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $86,479 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [856, 1400, 1455, 1579], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"The 2-year notes of Series BC-2022 were dated and issued June 30. They are due June 30, 2022, with interest payable on December 31 and June 30 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [854, 1579, 1457, 1926], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on June 23. Tenders totaled $113,050 million; Treasury accepted $46,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.193 percent with an equivalent price of $99.864327. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.193 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 94.81 percent. The median yield was 0.160 percent, and the low yield was 0.080\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [224, 1989, 395, 2020], \"page_id\": 50}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [450, 97, 1091, 127], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"BUREAU OF THE FISCAL SERVICE OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1293, 94, 1331, 127], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"43\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [386, 189, 1246, 231], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: APRIL-JUNE, continued\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 264, 770, 354], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $101 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $45,799 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 356, 772, 509], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $46,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $6,292 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series BC-2022 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 535, 492, 573], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Auction of 5-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 599, 770, 750], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"On June 18, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $47,000 million of 5-year notes. The issue was to refund $79,521 million of securities maturing June 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $86,479 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 752, 770, 940], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"The 5-year notes of Series AA-2025 were dated and issued June 30. They are due June 30, 2025, with interest payable on December 31 and June 30 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/4 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 940, 776, 1367], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on June 24. Tenders totaled $121,074 million; Treasury accepted $47,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.330 percent with an equivalent price of $99.603606. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.330 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 27.98 percent. The median yield was 0.288 percent, and the low yield was 0.220 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $15 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $46,985 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [184, 1370, 776, 1520], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $47,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $6,428 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series AA-2025 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [188, 1549, 490, 1584], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Auction of 7-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 1610, 769, 1763], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"On June 18, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $41,000 million of 7-year notes. The issue was to refund $79,521 million of securities maturing June 30 and to raise new cash of approximately $86,479 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [191, 1766, 776, 1893], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"The 7-year notes of Series M-2027 were dated and issued June 30. They are due June 30, 2027, with interest payable on December 31 and June 30 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 0-1/2 percent\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 266, 1446, 325], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [862, 328, 1444, 750], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12:00 noon ET for noncompetitive tenders and before 1:00 p.m. ET for competitive tenders on June 25. Tenders totaled $102,035 million; Treasury accepted $41,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 0.511 percent with an equivalent price of $99.924456. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 0.511 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 60.32 percent. The median yield was 0.465 percent, and the low yield was 0.080 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $2 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $40,998 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [860, 754, 1444, 910], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $41,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $5,608 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series M-2027 is $100.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 938, 1408, 971], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Auction of 105-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 997, 1446, 1278], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"On June 23, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $30,000 million of 105-day bills. They were issued June 30 and will mature October 13. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $30,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 24. Tenders totaled $100,462 million; Treasury accepted $30,001 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.150 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1301, 1404, 1341], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"Auction of 154-Day Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [858, 1367, 1443, 1648], \"page_id\": 51}], \"content\": \"On June 23, 2020, Treasury announced it would auction $35,000 million of 154-day bills. They were issued June 30 and will mature December 1. The issue was to raise new cash of approximately $35,000 million. Treasury auctioned the bills on June 24. Tenders totaled $112,721 million; Treasury accepted $35,001 million, including $2 million of noncompetitive tenders from the public. The high bank discount rate was 0.165 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\