 Act of January 30, 1934 codified at 31 United States Code 5302, which authorized establishment of a Treasury fund to be operated under the exclusive control of the Secretary, with approval of the President.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 483, 801, 575], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Subsequent amendment of the Gold Reserve Act modified the original purpose somewhat to reflect termination of the fixed exchange rate system.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 575, 803, 1124], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Section 4027 of H.R. 748, the Coronavirus Aid, Relief, and Economic Security Act (CARES Act), enacted on March 27, 2020 as Pub. Law 116-136, appropriated $500 billion to the Exchange Stabilization Fund (ESF), which the Secretary of the Treasury is authorized to use to make loans, loan guarantees, and other investments in support of eligible businesses, States, and municipalities and to provide the subsidy amounts necessary for such loans, loan guarantees, and other investments in accordance with the provisions of the Federal Credit Reform Act of 1990 (2 U.S.C. 661 et seq.). The CARES Act appropriation is used to fund the credit subsidy portion of loans, loan guarantees, and other investments authorized under section 4003 of the CARES Act, and the remaining portion of such disbursements is funded by borrowings from Treasury through the Bureau of Fiscal Service. This appropriated balance and borrowings from Treasury are held as a fund balance with Treasury until disbursed.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 1127, 803, 1254], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Resources of the fund include (a) Fund Balance, which reflects the appropriation from the CARES Act minus the net credit subsidy portion of all investments and expenditures for administrative expenses in support of the\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 269, 1494, 455], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"CARES Act, (b) U.S. Government securities (dollar balances), (c) special drawing rights -SDRs, and (d) foreign currencies. Principal sources of income -- or loss -- for the fund are profits -- or losses -- on SDRs and foreign exchange, interest earned on U.S Government and foreign securities, SDRs, and other non-CARES Act facilities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 462, 1494, 889], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Table ESF-1 presents the assets, liabilities, and capital of the fund. The figures are in U.S. dollars. Amounts and transactions pertaining to foreign currencies have been converted to U.S. dollars based on current exchange rates computed according to the accrual method of accounting. Investments are reported at cost. The capital account represents the original capital appropriated to the fund by Congress of $2 billion, minus a subsequent transfer of $1.8 billion to pay for the initial U.S. quota subscription to the International Monetary Fund. The additional appropriated capital represents the $500 billion appropriated under the CARES Act Sec 4003 minus transfers and expenditures. Conversion gains and losses are reflected in the cumulative net income --+ or loss -- account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 896, 1495, 1176], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"Table ESF-2 shows the results of operations for the current quarter and year-to-date. Figures are in U.S. dollars computed according to the accrual method. \\\"Profit --+ or loss -- on foreign exchange\\\" includes realized profits or losses. \\\"Adjustment for change in valuation of SDR holdings and allocations\\\" reflects net gain or loss on revaluation of SDR holdings and allocations for the quarter. CARES Act related administrative costs incurred in connection with the loans, loan guarantees and other investments are accrued.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1339, 594, 1372], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"See Table ESF-1 and ESF-2 on the following pages.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1994, 308, 2018], \"page_id\": 76}], \"content\": \"September 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [545, 92, 991, 132], \"page_id\": 77}], \"content\": \"EXCHANGE STABILIZATION FUND\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1455, 99, 1494, 127], \"page_id\": 77}], \"content\": \"69\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [364, 184, 1264, 233], \"page_id\": 77}], \"content\": \"TABLE ESF-1\\u2014Balances as of Mar. 31, 2020, and June 30, 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [461, 240, 1177, 269], \"page_id\": 77}], \"content\": \"[In thousands of dollars. Source: Office of the Assistant Secretary of the Treasury for Management]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 273, 1492, 1233], \"page_id\": 77}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Assets, liabilities, and capital</th><th>Mar. 31, 2020</th><th>Apr. 1, 2020, through June 30, 2020</th><th>June 30, 2020</th></tr><tr><td><b>Assets</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>U.S. dollars:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Held with Treasury:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fund Balance</td><td>500,000,000</td><td>(10,046,205)</td><td>489,953,795</td></tr><tr><td>U.S. Government securities</td><td>22,687,568</td><td>(11,515,264)</td><td>11,172,304</td></tr><tr><td>Special drawing rights 1</td><td>50,135,749</td><td>420,577</td><td>50,556,326</td></tr><tr><td>Economic Recovery Program Investments</td><td>-</td><td>