{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775347083-c6OpN7VRauTCBHsxSm9a","role":"assistant","created":1775347102,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the data for fiscal years 2010-2024. Let me collect the receipts and outlays for each year:\n\nFrom 2015 bulletin (page 18):\n- 2010: Receipts = 2,161,728; Outlays = 3,455,931\n- 2011: Receipts = 2,302,495; Outlays = 3,598,086\n- 2012: Receipts = 2,449,092; Outlays = 3,538,447\n- 2013: Receipts = 2,773,979; Outlays = 3,454,254\n- 2014: Receipts = 3,020,847; Outlays = 3,504,199\n\nFrom 2020 bulletin (page 21):\n- 2015: Receipts = 3,248,722; Outlays = 3,687,623\n- 2016: Receipts = 3,266,689; Outlays = 3,854,101\n- 2017: Receipts = 3,314,893; Outlays = 3,980,720\n- 2018: Receipts = 3,328,745; Outlays = 4,107,741\n- 2019: Receipts = 3,462,195; Outlays = 4,446,583\n\nFrom 2024 bulletin (page 21):\n- 2020: Receipts = 3,419,955; Outlays = 6,551,871\n- 2021: Receipts = 4,045,980; Outlays = 6,818,159\n- 2022: Receipts = 4,896,119; Outlays = 6,271,508\n- 2023: Receipts = 4,439,283; Outlays = 6,134,433\n\nFrom 2025 bulletin (page 22):\n\n\n- 2024: Receipts = 4,918,737; Outlays = 6,751,553\n\nI need to apply the Hodrick-Prescott filter with a smoothing parameter of 100 to extract trend components from the receipts and outlays series. Then I'll compute the structural balance as trend receipts minus trend outlays, and the actual balance as receipts minus outlays for each fiscal year from 2010 through 2024. Finally, I'll calculate the three values for FY 2024: the actual balance, structural balance, and the gap between them.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_c51b5bfd1da84ebfad86964f","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Data for FY 2010-2024 (in millions)\nfiscal_years = list(range(2010, 2025))\n\n# Receipts and outlays data from the bulletins\nreceipts = [\n    2161728,  # 2010\n    2302495,  # 2011\n    2449092,  # 2012\n    2773979,  # 2013\n    3020847,  # 2014\n    3248722,  # 2015\n    3266689,  # 2016\n    3314893,  # 2017\n    3328745,  # 2018\n    3462195,  # 2019\n    3419955,  # 2020\n    4045980,  # 2021\n    4896119,  # 2022\n    4439283,  # 2023\n    4918737,  # 2024\n]\n\noutlays = [\n    3455931,  # 2010\n    3598086,  # 2011\n    3538447,  # 2012\n    3454254,  # 2013\n    3504199,  # 2014\n    3687623,  # 2015\n    3854101,  # 2016\n    3980720,  # 2017\n    4107741,  # 2018\n    4446583,  # 2019\n    6551871,  # 2020\n    6818159,  # 2021\n    6271508,  # 2022\n    6134433,  # 2023\n    6751553,  # 2024\n]\n\nprint(\"FY\\tReceipts\\tOutlays\\tActual Balance\")\nfor i, fy in enumerate(fiscal_years):\n    actual_balance = receipts[i] - outlays[i]\n    print(f\"{fy}\\t{receipts[i]:,}\\t{outlays[i]:,}\\t{actual_balance:,}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
