{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775347109-ImKnxZ6GDX3cgyakkExs","role":"assistant","created":1775347130,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me implement the Hodrick-Prescott filter manually. It's a smoothing technique that decomposes a time series into a trend component and a cyclical component. The HP filter finds the trend τ_t that minimizes:\n\n∑(y_t - τ_t)² + λ∑((τ_{t+1} - τ_t) - (τ_t - τ_{t-1}))²\n\nFor annual data, λ=100 is standard.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_839f80ec984b4fcdb1711b17","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Manual HP Filter implementation\n\ndef hp_filter(y, lamb=100):\n    \"\"\"\n    Hodrick-Prescott filter\n    y: time series\n    lamb: smoothing parameter\n    Returns: trend component\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(y)\n    \n    # Create the second difference matrix\n    # D is (n-2) x n\n    D = np.zeros((n-2, n))\n    for i in range(n-2):\n        D[i, i] = 1\n        D[i, i+1] = -2\n        D[i, i+2] = 1\n    \n    # Solve for trend: (I + lamb*D'D)^-1 * y\n    I = np.eye(n)\n    # We need to compute (I + lamb*D'D)^-1\n    # D'D is a tridiagonal matrix\n    DTD = D.T @ D\n    \n    # This gives us the matrix to invert\n    B = I + lamb * DTD\n    \n    # Use numpy to solve the system\n    trend = np.linalg.solve(B, y)\n    \n    return trend\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n# Data for FY 2010-2024 (in millions)\nfiscal_years = list(range(2010, 2025))\n\n# Receipts and outlays data from the bulletins\nreceipts = np.array([\n    2161728,  # 2010\n    2302495,  # 2011\n    2449092,  # 2012\n    2773979,  # 2013\n    3020847,  # 2014\n    3248722,  # 2015\n    3266689,  # 2016\n    3314893,  # 2017\n    3328745,  # 2018\n    3462195,  # 2019\n    3419955,  # 2020\n    4045980,  # 2021\n    4896119,  # 2022\n    4439283,  # 2023\n    4918737,  # 2024\n])\n\noutlays = np.array([\n    3455931,  # 2010\n    3598086,  # 2011\n    3538447,  # 2012\n    3454254,  # 2013\n    3504199,  # 2014\n    3687623,  # 2015\n    3854101,  # 2016\n    3980720,  # 2017\n    4107741,  # 2018\n    4446583,  # 2019\n    6551871,  # 2020\n    6818159,  # 2021\n    6271508,  # 2022\n    6134433,  # 2023\n    6751553,  # 2024\n])\n\n# Apply HP filter with lambda=100\ntrend_receipts = hp_filter(receipts, lamb=100)\ntrend_outlays = hp_filter(outlays, lamb=100)\n\nprint(\"FY\\tActual Rec\\tTrend Rec\\tActual Out\\tTrend Out\\tActual Bal\\tStructural Bal\")\nfor i, fy in enumerate(fiscal_years):\n    actual_balance = receipts[i] - outlays[i]\n    structural_balance = trend_receipts[i] - trend_outlays[i]\n    print(f\"{fy}\\t{receipts[i]:,}\\t{trend_receipts[i]:,.0f}\\t{outlays[i]:,}\\t{trend_outlays[i]:,.0f}\\t{actual_balance:,}\\t{structural_balance:,.0f}\")\n\n# FY 2024 values\nfy2024_idx = 14  # 2024 is the 15th year (index 14)\nactual_2024 = receipts[fy2024_idx] - outlays[fy2024_idx]\nstructural_2024 = trend_receipts[fy2024_idx] - trend_outlays[fy2024_idx]\ngap_2024 = abs(actual_2024 - structural_2024)\n\nprint(\"\\n--- FY 2024 Results ---\")\nprint(f\"Actual Balance (FY 2024): {actual_2024:,.0f} million\")\nprint(f\"Structural Balance (FY 2024): {structural_2024:,.0f} million\")\nprint(f\"Absolute Gap (FY 2024): {gap_2024:,.0f} million\")\n\n# Round to nearest whole number\nprint(\"\\n--- FY 2024 Rounded Results ---\")\nprint(f\"Actual Balance (rounded): {round(actual_2024):,} million\")\nprint(f\"Structural Balance (rounded): {round(structural_2024):,} million\")\nprint(f\"Absolute Gap (rounded): {round(gap_2024):,} million\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
